            <ArticleTitle>[Acute pelvic pain syndrome. Diagnostic and therapeutic approach in women].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute pelvic pain is a common syndrome in women and is an emergency. Management requires rapid diagnostic evaluation to enable immediate treatment. Blood tests (beta-HCG assay, etc.), bacteriological studies and pelvic ultrasonography may be required. Gynecological problems are the commonest etiology: ectopic pregnancy, miscarriage, PID. The possibility nevertheless remains of appendicitis, sigmoid diverticulitis, UTI or renal colic, all of which are medical or surgical emergencies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
